-- title:
--   Maximal ideals generate along base change to the geometric fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ lying over $p$, in the sense that $p$ belongs to the nonunits of $A$. Let $\mathfrak X$ be a `DRModelPackage` for $p$, i.e. a bundle of properties and structures for the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` of the full modular function field over $\mathbf Z$ and its morphism `DRModel.toBase p` to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed (hence perfect) field of characteristic $p$ and $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ a ring homomorphism. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain together with a ring isomorphism $e_O$ onto the preimage of $A$ in the fixed field of the inertia subgroup `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` (the image in $\operatorname{Aut}(\overline{\mathbf Q}/\mathbf Q)$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$ inside its decomposition subgroup), such that the maximal ideal of $O$ is generated by $p$; let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to k$ be a ring homomorphism which, via $e_O$ and the inclusion of the fixed field into $\overline{\mathbf Q}$, agrees with $\mathrm{red}$. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two morphisms $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,k$ and $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\,k$ of the package into the base change of `DRModel p` to $k$, so that the two images of $n$ in that $k$-scheme coincide. Assume that this common image, pushed by the base-change morphism `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ` to the base change of `DRModel p` to $O$, has residue field generated by $O$: the composite of $O \cong \Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} O)$ with the global-sections map of the second projection, the germ map into the stalk at that point, and the residue map, is surjective. The conclusion is the conjunction of two statements, one for each branch: at the image of $n$ under $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,k$ composed with the first projection, and at the image under $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\,k$ composed with the second projection, the ideal generated by the image of the maximal ideal of the stalk of the $O$-model under the stalk map of `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ` is the maximal ideal of the corresponding stalk of the $k$-model.
--
--   This is the unramifiedness of the base change from the valuation ring of the inertia field to the algebraically closed residue field, read at a crossing point of the two labelled components of the geometric fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model: the maximal ideal downstairs generates the maximal ideal upstairs at each of the two branch points. It supplies the two local inputs used in the determination of node coordinates on the fibre and in the comparison of widths for the resolved model package.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRModelPackage_map_maximalIdeal_stalkMap_baseChangeMap_eq_of_inertia_grain.lean

